        <briefdescription>
<para>Handles the --init command line option. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Reads the family name from --init. The manifest file name derives from the family name and lands in the current directory. When the file exists, it is read and validated; otherwise the default manifest for the family is the starting document.</para>
<para>Three tables are added when missing. The glyphs table is built from the first declared weight whose glyph sheet exists on disk, or from the default printable ASCII range when no sheet exists. The guides table and the colour table take their default rows. The manifest is written only when it gained a table.</para>
<para>Then, for every weight declared in the manifest&apos;s font table that has a glyph sheet path, the weight&apos;s glyph sheet is written, reconciled against the glyphs table. A weight without a sheet on disk gets one.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>args</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The parsed command line arguments; must carry --init. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
